WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.311 --> 00:00:02.600
(gentle music)

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:05.040
- I'm here at the
Olympic Village in Tokyo.

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.280
And this is where around
18,000 athletes and officials

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:10.040
will be staying during the games.

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:11.930
But the concern is that there could be

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:14.890
a super spreader event at the Olympics.

00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:18.673
It's raised a huge logistical
challenge for the organizers.

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:22.470
You can't really create a
kind of bubble situation

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:23.690
for the Olympics.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:25.000
So what they're doing is

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.760
they're creating controlled zones

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:29.632
where they don't want people to leave.

00:00:29.632 --> 00:00:32.215
(upbeat music)

00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:40.710
Controlling people

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:43.230
and making sure that
they follow various rules

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:45.530
will be a huge challenge.

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:46.580
So we are going to see

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:49.040
how the organizers plan to make sure

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:51.510
the world's biggest sporting
event during the pandemic

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:53.233
doesn't become a COVID hotspot.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.410
So this is where the
athletes are gonna be eating.

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:01.720
Of course, the dining
area is one of the places

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:05.170
at the Olympics where people
like to socialize normally.

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:07.500
But that's one thing that
the organizers want to avoid.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.930
It's a potential hotspot
for virus transmission.

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:14.200
So most of the athletes will
be eating by themselves.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:15.350
This is the fitness center,

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:18.270
and a special precaution
is here as well of course.

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:20.070
The organizers here say

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:22.770
that they will be asking
athletes to wear masks.

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:25.540
There's quite aggressive
air circulation as well.

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:27.020
But the machines are very close together.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:30.290
So this is a place where
they are saying that

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:31.960
if athletes come,

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:33.010
and it is very busy,

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:35.160
they will be turning
them away at the door.

00:01:37.010 --> 00:01:38.070
These are the condominiums

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:39.410
that the athletes are gonna be staying

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:40.243
in here in the village.

00:01:40.243 --> 00:01:43.090
And we can get up to eight
athletes in one apartment.

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:45.757
(gentle music)

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:58.760
This is an event that's
spread all over the country.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:01.470
It's all around the Greater Tokyo region.

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:05.230
It's even 500 miles away
in Hokkaido in the north,

00:02:05.230 --> 00:02:07.490
where the marathon is going to be held.

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:10.750
So the goal is to create
this kind of archipelago

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:13.280
of controlled zones across Japan.

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:15.850
When people travel
between the village say,

00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:18.460
and the Olympic stadium or other venues,

00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:21.870
there'll be dedicated bus and taxi links.

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:22.970
There will be punishments

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:27.230
that will be imposed on
people that go into the city.

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:29.020
The organizers even said that

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:32.920
they want people to have
the GPS tracking function

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:35.656
turned on the smartphone
when they come in.

00:02:35.656 --> 00:02:38.323
(gentle music)

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:04.620
The organizers have come up
with some very strict rules

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:07.720
about what people can and cannot do.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:09.360
In general, in Japan,

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:11.300
people do follow the rules.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:13.630
But there's some concern here in Japan

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:15.090
that people coming from overseas

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:17.020
will be a bit more cavalier.

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:20.450
So you have quite a large
movement of people around.

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:22.010
And that's a challenge

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:25.480
to make sure that those
people don't spread the virus

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:26.920
amongst each other,

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:29.220
and that we don't have a sharp increase

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:32.842
which could put the
Olympics really into crisis.

00:03:32.842 --> 00:03:35.059
(gentle music)

